{
 "notes": {
  "transfer": "DQN-SA and DQN-I cannot run at another size: their input dimension is fixed by the number of gNBs. Rules have no learned part; the static rule's threshold was chosen in Env A at 3 gNBs and its 37-gNB compliance is sla37.rule_static. The tuned local rule was never carried across sizes in Env A.",
  "m76_m96_rule_identical": true,
  "private_training": "Only AXIOM was trained federated (measured). For the others the entry follows from the training design stated in the paper (Sec. 4, Table 3): MAPPO's critic reads every gNB's features, DQN-SA is one learner over the joint state, DQN-I trains each gNB on its own requests, and the rules learn no model."
 },
